course: dictionary
lesson: 15476
title: A clever plan
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A stratagem is a clever plan or trick. People use a stratagem to get what they want, or to fool an enemy. The word is a noun, and its plural is stratagems.
explain: Read the context to find the meaning. «Badger's stratagem was to enter Toad Hall by the secret tunnel while the weasels were feasting.» The words secret tunnel and while the weasels were feasting show that the plan is sneaky and clever, so stratagem must mean a clever plan.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Badger's clever plan was to enter Toad Hall by the secret tunnel while the weasels were feasting.» It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: «Stratagem» means a clever plan or trick.
fact: Stratagems appear in stories, games, sport and history.
fact: The Trojan Horse was a famous stratagem in Greek legend.
fact: In chess and sport, a stratagem is a smart plan to win.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad uses many stratagems to escape from prison.
exercise: «The fox's stratagem was to lure the hens out with a trail of corn.» What is a stratagem? | A loud noise in the farmyard | *A clever plan or trick | A type of corn | A kind of hen house
exercise: «Mia's stratagem to win the race was to hide a map under her shirt.» What does stratagem mean here? | A map of the countryside | *A clever plan to get what she wants | A running race | A rule that everyone must follow
exercise: The Trojan Horse was a famous stratagem in Greek legend. Which of these is the best example of a stratagem? | A horse's saddle and bridle | A picture of a horse on a wall | A horse that won a race at the fair | *A wooden horse hiding soldiers, used to fool the enemy
test: «The chess player used a stratagem to trap her opponent's queen.» What does stratagem mean? | *A clever plan or trick to win | A clever plan or trick | A quiet place to sit | A kind of chess piece
test: «Toad's many stratagems helped him escape from prison.» What did Toad's stratagems do? | *Helped him escape by clever plans | Made him very hungry | Gave him a new home | Made him sleep all day
exam: «The general's stratagem fooled the enemy, who thought the army had gone home.» What does stratagem mean? | *A clever plan or trick to fool an enemy | A loud cheer after a battle | A wet, grey day | A large army
